course: dictionary
lesson: 9483
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around the word. «She ordered a steak with chips and salad.» The chips and salad tell you steak is food, so it must mean a meal of meat.
explain: «The tuna steak was pink and firm, cut from the fish.» Here steak is not beef. The clue is tuna, a fish, so a steak can be a thick slice of fish too. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Sometimes the place tells you the meaning. «Mum made a steak and kidney pie with cheap chopped beef.» In the UK, steak can mean cheaper chopped beef for pies and stews. The pie is the clue. When the context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A steak is a thick, flat slice of good meat, usually beef, cooked by grilling or frying.
fact: A steak can also be a thick slice of fish, such as salmon or tuna.
fact: In the UK, steak can mean cheaper chopped beef used in pies and stews, as in steak and kidney pie.
fact: Steak is often a special meal, and you can have it rare, medium or well done.
fact: French menus use the same idea: «steak haché» is a minced-beef patty, not a thick slice.
exercise: «She ordered a steak with chips and salad.» What is a steak here? | A cake filled with cream | A small grey bird | A dog's lead | *A thick, flat slice of good meat, usually beef
exercise: «The tuna steak was pink and firm, cut from the fish.» What kind of steak is this? | A slice of beef from the cow's back | A cheap meat used only for soup | A tin of beans | *A thick slice of fish
exercise: In a UK shop, a pie is labelled «steak and kidney». What does steak mean on that label? | A dessert with fruit | *Cheaper chopped beef used in pies and stews | A kind of bread roll | A thick slice of fish
test: In «rare steak», which word tells you how the steak is cooked? | *rare | meat | steak | the
test: The French menu says «steak haché». Which meaning fits best? | *A minced-beef patty | A thick slice of tuna | A cheap cut for stew | A kind of chips
exam: «Dad grilled a thick, flat slice of beef on the barbecue.» Which meaning of steak fits? | A dog's lead | *A thick, flat slice of good meat, usually beef | A cake filled with cream | A small grey bird
